  "note": "Errata 303. Room 20's exterior depth (258 at y705) was the graybox's, and the plates came back with the buildings drawn smaller: the church's door is 180 px tall at the head of its steps and the registrar's 160, so a man of that depth walking up to them would be taller than either. Read off the plate instead: the horizon at y326, where the road meets the town, and a man at the foot of the church steps (y630) at 0.85 of its door, 152. 0.5 x (y - 326), from y600 (137), the back of the alley's mouth, to the front (266). The lane's doors are 235 px and keep the old depth."
